cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this harness, please cite the repository (and the associated paper once it is published)."
type: software
title: "LLM-assisted EEG preprocessing harness"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of a state-conditioned EEG preprocessing decision:
  a record is compressed into a fingerprint and mapped to a state set, an action
  is selected from a finite candidate set by a knowledge graph, a calibration
  memory of measured gains, and an optional language model with pre- and
  post-gates, and decisions are scored by paired downstream measurement.
authors:
  - family-names: Wan
    given-names: Zirui
version: 1.2
date-released: 2026-11-26
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/qwedcccq/Wan-Zirui"
keywords:
  - EEG
  - preprocessing
  - brain-computer interface
  - large language model
  - decision support
